              "delta": "Reasoning:\n_The user is asking about Foundry's client retainer strategy. I have this information directly in my context from the COMPANY OPERATING CONTEXT section. Let me answer from what I know._\n\n_From the context:_\n_- \"Six retainers a year is a ceiling, not a target\" - Foundry takes six retainers per year on purpose_\n_- The reasoning: \"Foundry economics work because we say no to most inbound. Past six concurrent retainers, founder-time-per-client falls below the threshold that makes our work distinguishable from a normal growth shop. Six is a hard cap, not an aspiration.\"_\n_- Also from the pricing belief: \"Pricing — we pick six clients a year. _\n\n_Beyond the six-client cap, Foundry's model is built on owning their own distribution rather than relying on external channels, and they're selective about which projects they take on—they'll turn down work that doesn't genuinely interest them, even if it means leaving money on the table._",
